-- title:
--   Level automorphisms of K₁· F₀ fixing j(qτ)
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime with $q\ge 5$ and $M'\ge 1$ with $q\nmid M'$, and write $F=$ `fieldBar q M'` for the subfield of $\overline{\mathbb Q}((X))$ generated over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ by the coefficientwise images of the function field of $X_H$ of level $q^2M'$, where $H\le(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times$ is the kernel of reduction to $(\mathbb Z/q)^\times$; assume the corresponding $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-base change `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` of the level-$M'$ full modular function field is contained in $F$. Let $k_0\subseteq\overline{\mathbb Q}$ be an intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q$, let $K_1$ be an intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/k_0$ with $K_1/k_0$ finite, and let $A_1$ be a valuation subring of $K_1$; $F$ carries the $k_0$-algebra structure coming from the constants. Let $F_0$ be an intermediate field of $F/k_0$ such that: $\overline{\mathbb Q}\cdot F_0=F$ (the join of $F_0$ with the $k_0$-subfield generated by the image of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ is everything); $F_0$ is stable under `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` for every primitive $q$-th root of unity $\zeta'\in\overline{\mathbb Q}$ and every $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$, where `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` is a $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-algebra automorphism of $F$ satisfying the $q$-expansion condition `IsLevelAutBar` (it matches, under each embedding of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ in $\mathbb C$ sending $\zeta'$ to $e^{2\pi i/q}$, the effect of `conjElem q γ` on ratios of integral $q$-expansions of modular forms of level $\Gamma_H(q^2M')$), and is the identity if no such automorphism exists; for every intermediate field $K'$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/k_0$ with $K'/k_0$ finite, every $K'$-linearly independent family $c_1,\dots,c_m\in\overline{\mathbb Q}$ and all $a_1,\dots,a_m$ in the subfield $K'\cdot F_0$ generated over $k_0$ by the image of $K'$ and by $F_0$, the relation $\sum_i c_i a_i=0$ forces $a_i=0$ for all $i$; and every element of $F$ whose Laurent series lies in the image of `coeffEmb` (that is, has rational coefficients) belongs to $F_0$. Put $T_1=K_1\cdot F_0$, the join of $F_0$ with the $k_0$-subfield generated by the image of $K_1$, and suppose $T_1$ is an $A_1$-algebra whose structure map is, on the nose, the inclusion $A_1\subseteq K_1\subseteq\overline{\mathbb Q}\to F$. Finally let $j_1\in T_1$ have as image in $F$ the element with Laurent series `coeffEmb` of `jq`, the $q$-expansion of the modular invariant. Then there exists $j'\in T_1$ whose Laurent series is `coeffEmb` of `qExpand ℚ q jq` (the $q$-expansion of $j$ with exponents multiplied by $q$) such that $j'$ is integral over $A_1[j_1]$ and $j_1$ is integral over $A_1[j']$, and such that every $g$ in the subgroup of $\mathrm{Aut}_{\overline{\mathbb Q}}(F)$ generated by the automorphisms `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` ($\zeta$ a primitive $q$-th root of unity, $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$) admits an $A_1$-algebra automorphism $\sigma$ of $T_1$ with: $\sigma$ acting on elements of $T_1$ as $g$ does, $\sigma^{-1}$ acting as $g^{-1}$, $\sigma(j')=j'$, $b$ integral over $A_1[j_1]$ if and only if $\sigma b$ is, $b$ integral over $A_1[1/j']$ if and only if $\sigma b$ is, and, for every place $P$ of $F$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ (a valuation subring of $F$ containing the constants, different from $F$, and a principal ideal ring) whose residue field is generated by $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, the translate $g\cdot P$ has the same property, with $(g\cdot P)$-evaluation of $gf$ equal to the $P$-evaluation of $f$ and $gf$ in the valuation subring of $g\cdot P$ exactly when $f$ lies in that of $P$, for all $f\in F$.
--
--   This is the working form of the statement that the level automorphisms act on the two-chart integral model of the modular curve: they do not fix the modular invariant $j_1$ nor stabilise its pole chart, but they fix the companion function $j'$ with $q$-expansion $j(q\tau)$, and $j_1$, $j'$ are mutually integral by the modular equation $\Phi_q(j_1,j')=0$, so that the finite chart ring of $j_1$ and the pole chart ring of $j'$ are stable. It is used in the descent arguments over the valuation ring $A_1$ that produce level automorphisms moving a given point into a prescribed chart, and in the identification of the Igusa ring.
